{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the man knew Eve his wife.</b> After he saw that he had been banished from the Garden of Eden on account of his sin, and death had been decreed upon him so that he would not live forever, he needed to unite with Eve for the perpetuation of the species, to leave offspring after him. And know that the conjugal act in the language of the Torah is called 'knowing' (ידיעה), and the reason is that the seed comes from the brain, which is the seat of wisdom and knowledge. Moreover, the lust for conjugal relations had its cause in the Tree of Knowledge, and therefore it is called by the name 'knowing.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:59.982536453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}